{
  "id": "unicode-to-shree-san7",
  "name": "Unicode -\u003E Shree-Lipi 7.0 Sanskrit",
  "sourceFontId": "mangal",
  "targetFontId": "shree-san7",
  "sourceType": "unicode",
  "targetType": "legacy",
  "preRules": [
    {
      "pattern": "\u0958",
      "replace": "\u0915\u093C",
      "note": "\u0958 is \u0915 \u002B nukta: the Sanskrit fonts have no nukta (Shree\u0027s Sanskrit composer drops it), so \u0915, and the nukta is reported."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u0959",
      "replace": "\u0916\u093C",
      "note": "\u0959 is \u0916 \u002B nukta: the Sanskrit fonts have no nukta (Shree\u0027s Sanskrit composer drops it), so \u0916, and the nukta is reported."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u095A",
      "replace": "\u0917\u093C",
      "note": "\u095A is \u0917 \u002B nukta: the Sanskrit fonts have no nukta (Shree\u0027s Sanskrit composer drops it), so \u0917, and the nukta is reported."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u095B",
      "replace": "\u091C\u093C",
      "note": "\u095B is \u091C \u002B nukta: the Sanskrit fonts have no nukta (Shree\u0027s Sanskrit composer drops it), so \u091C, and the nukta is reported."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u095C",
      "replace": "\u0921\u093C",
      "note": "\u095C is \u0921 \u002B nukta: the Sanskrit fonts have no nukta (Shree\u0027s Sanskrit composer drops it), so \u0921, and the nukta is reported."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u095D",
      "replace": "\u0922\u093C",
      "note": "\u095D is \u0922 \u002B nukta: the Sanskrit fonts have no nukta (Shree\u0027s Sanskrit composer drops it), so \u0922, and the nukta is reported."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u095E",
      "replace": "\u092B\u093C",
      "note": "\u095E is \u092B \u002B nukta: the Sanskrit fonts have no nukta (Shree\u0027s Sanskrit composer drops it), so \u092B, and the nukta is reported."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u095F",
      "replace": "\u092F\u093C",
      "note": "\u095F is \u092F \u002B nukta: the Sanskrit fonts have no nukta (Shree\u0027s Sanskrit composer drops it), so \u092F, and the nukta is reported."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u0929",
      "replace": "\u0928\u093C",
      "note": "\u0929 is \u0928 \u002B nukta: the Sanskrit fonts have no nukta (Shree\u0027s Sanskrit composer drops it), so \u0928, and the nukta is reported."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u0931",
      "replace": "\u0930\u093C",
      "note": "\u0931 is \u0930 \u002B nukta: the Sanskrit fonts have no nukta (Shree\u0027s Sanskrit composer drops it), so \u0930, and the nukta is reported."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u0934",
      "replace": "\u0933\u093C",
      "note": "\u0934 is \u0933 \u002B nukta: the Sanskrit fonts have no nukta (Shree\u0027s Sanskrit composer drops it), so \u0933, and the nukta is reported."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "([\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F])\u093C",
      "replace": "\u093C$1",
      "note": "Nukta: the Sanskrit fonts have none; moved before its letter, where the pairs leave it out and report it."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u094D(?:\u200C|(?![\u0900-\u0963\u0971-\u097F\u200D\u200C]))",
      "replace": "\uFDD4",
      "note": "A visible virama is the halant 6F (U\u002BFDD4 marks it for the pairs): \u094D\u002BZWNJ, and a virama that ends a word - before a space, punctuation, a danda, a digit, anything but a letter or sign of the script or a joiner, or at the end of the text. Every Unicode font draws a word-final virama as a visible halant; the half form the composer answers for a bare virama is only what it shows while it waits for the next letter."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "(?\u003C![\u094D\u200D\u093C])\u0930\u094D(?![\u200D\u094D])(?:((?:\u093C?[\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F]\u094D\u200D?)*\u093C?[\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F](?!\u094D)|[\u0904-\u0914\u0960\u0961\u0972-\u0977\u0950])|(?![\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F\u093C]))([\u0901\u0902\u093E\u093F\u0940\u0941\u0942\u0943\u0944\u0945\u0947\u0948\u0949\u094B\u094C\u0951\u0952\u0962\u0963]*)",
      "replace": "$1$2\uFDD0",
      "note": "Reph: \u0930\u094D before a letter is written after the letter and its signs (before a visarga; and before a sign the fonts have no glyph for, which the table passes through - Word draws it on a dotted circle of its own, and the reph belongs on its letter); U\u002BFDD0 marks it for the pairs. \u0930\u094D\u002BZWJ is the eyelash ra, \u0931\u094D the half ra."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "([\u0936\u0924]\u094D\u0930\u094D)(?=\u092F[\u093E\u0940-\u094C\u0962\u0963])",
      "replace": "$1\u200D",
      "note": "\u0936\u094D\u0930\u094D\u092F \u0924\u094D\u0930\u094D\u092F with a vowel sign: the half \u0936\u094D\u0930\u094D \u0924\u094D\u0930\u094D and \u092F, as with a ZWJ."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "(?\u003C=[\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F]\u094D\u200D?\u093C?[\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F]\u094D\u200D?\u093C?[\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F])\u094D\u092F(?![\u093F\u0900-\u0903\u094D\u200D\uFDD0\uFDD2\uFDD6\uFDD8\uFDD7\uFDDA])",
      "replace": "\uFDD8",
      "note": "Ya-sign after a conjunct of three letters or more, with no sign: E7 (U\u002BFDD8 marks it)."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "(?\u003C=[\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F]\u094D\u200D?\u093C?[\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F])\u094D\u092F(?![\u093F\u0900-\u0903\u094D\u200D\uFDD0\uFDD2\uFDD6\uFDD8\uFDD7\uFDDA])",
      "replace": "\uFDD6",
      "note": "Ya-sign after a conjunct of two letters, with no sign or a vowel sign: E7 (U\u002BFDD6 marks it; \u0924\u094D\u0924\u094D\u092F is written with the half \u0924\u094D\u0924 there)."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "(?\u003C=[\u091F\u0920\u0921\u0922])\u094D\u092F(?![\u200D]|\u094D(?!\u0930))",
      "replace": "\uFDDA",
      "note": "Ya-sign: after \u091F \u0920 \u0921 \u0922 \u094D\u092F is always the ya-sign F7, in place of the spacer 3E (U\u002BFDDA marks it)."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u094D\u092F(?=[\u093E\u0940-\u094C\u0962\u0963])",
      "replace": "\uFDD7",
      "note": "Ya-sign with a vowel sign (not the i-sign): E7 (U\u002BFDD7 marks it)."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u094D\u092F(?![\u093F\u0900-\u0903\u094D\u200D\uFDD0\uFDD2\uFDD6\uFDD8\uFDD7\uFDDA])",
      "replace": "\uFDD2",
      "note": "Ya-sign: \u094D\u092F alone is the ya-sign E7 (U\u002BFDD2 marks it) - but before \u093F \u0902 \u0901 \u0903, a reph or the ra-sign the composer writes the half letter and \u092F."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u094D\u0930(?!\u200D|\u094D)",
      "replace": "\uFDD3",
      "note": "Ra-sign: \u094D\u0930 after a letter (U\u002BFDD3 marks it for the pairs)."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "(?\u003C=[\u0915\u0916\u0918\u091A\u091C\u091D\u0927\u092A\u092B\u092C\u092D\u092E\u0935])\u094D\u0928(?![\u094D\u200D])",
      "replace": "\uFDD9",
      "note": "Na-sign: \u094D\u0928 after \u0915 \u0916 \u0918 \u091A \u091C \u091D \u0927 \u092A \u092B \u092C \u092D \u092E \u0935 is the subscript 6E (U\u002BFDD9 marks it for the pairs); other letters take their half form (or halant) and \u0928."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "((?:\u093C?[\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F]\u094D\u200D?)*\u093C?[\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F](?:[\uFDD3\uFDD2\uFDD6\uFDD7\uFDD8\uFDD9\uFDDA])*)\u093F",
      "replace": "\u093F$1",
      "note": "The i-sign is written before its letter or conjunct (Unicode logical order -\u003E visual order)."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "\u094D(?![\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F\u093C\u200D])",
      "replace": "\u094D\uFDD5",
      "note": "A virama before a vowel letter or a sign (a word-final one is the halant, above): the composer writes the half form it is waiting with (U\u002BFDD5 marks it for the pairs)."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "([\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F])\u094D(?!\u0930)(?=(?:\u093C?[\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F]\u094D)\u002B(?:\uFDD5|\u093C?[\u0915-\u0939\u0958-\u095F]))",
      "replace": "$1\u094D\u200D",
      "note": "A conjunct with a virama after it (waiting for its next letter, or with one more) is written as half letters, not as a ligature - the composer breaks \u0915\u094D\u0915 into \u0915\u094D \u0915\u094D when a link follows: as if each virama but the last had a ZWJ."
    }
  ],
